<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Szeregy Szare    unloading   corn	     25,005     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  18,045</p>
<p>				     soya	     14,317</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	unloading   corn		4,336     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	    15,927</p>
<p>Ahmet Fatoglu    unloading   sunflower meal  2,600     Europe</p>
<p>Sanem		arrived     barley	    4,972     Europe</p>
<p>Volgodo 5023     arrived     rapeseeds	 3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Sormovsky 47     28/10	 bran wheat	1,500     Europe</p>
<p>Sormovsky 17     29/10	 feed wheat	2,860     Europe</p>
<p>Golden Sky	 30/10	 barley	   23,909     U.S.</p>
<p>Sormovsky 10	2/11	 barley	    3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Wave	5/11	 corn	     32,450     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   9,072</p>
<p>				     wheat	    19,300</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	10/11	 na		 60,000     U.S.</p>
